-- title:
--   Choosing one index where finitely many limits are nearly attained
-- statement:
--   Let $I$ be finite and $l$ a nontrivial filter on $J$. Let $e_i>0$, $a_i\ge1-e_i$, $g_i(j)\to a_i$ along $l$ for each $i$, $D(j)\to0$ along $l$, and $M>0$. Then there is $j$ with
--   $$
--   g_i(j)\ge1-2e_i\ \ (\forall i),\qquad D(j)\le M .
--   $$
--
--   This chooses one terminal point that works for all detectors of a finite truncation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Nonexpansive/CommonTerminal.lean#L25-L45

